<Editorial
  title="How Tagrivo is supported."
  description="A clear explanation of affiliate links, editorial independence, and what a purchase through a link can mean."
>
  <p>
    <strong>Last updated: October 29, 2026.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Tagrivo is supported in part by affiliate commissions. When you follow an identified affiliate
    link and make a qualifying purchase, we may earn a commission. Tagrivo does not add a fee to
    your purchase.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Participation remains subject to Amazon's program requirements and review. These links do not
    mean that Amazon endorses Tagrivo or has granted final approval of this website.
  </p>
  <h2>How to recognize an affiliate link</h2>
  <p>
    Amazon purchase links are labeled <strong>Paid link</strong> beside the link text. Those links
    are marked as sponsored in the page markup. A link to a manufacturer's specifications or support
    documentation is provided as evidence and is not an affiliate purchase link in this edition.
  </p>
  <h2>What commissions do not buy</h2>
  <p>
    Payment does not determine whether a model is compatible with your device, make it meet a
    budget, or remove a limitation from an analysis. The Finder's eligibility rules use product
    facts and your answers, not affiliate commissions.
  </p>
  <p>
    We do not offer paid placement in the initial shortlist. We do not invent reviews, testimonials,
    or hands-on testing. See our <a href="/methodology/">editorial methodology</a> for the
    boundaries of the current research.
  </p>
  <h2>Prices, availability, and other websites</h2>
  <p>
    Retailer prices and availability can change. A dated manufacturer price is identified as such.
    Calculator defaults are illustrative estimates. Always confirm the exact model, total price,
    delivery terms, and return policy at the destination website before buying.
  </p>
  <p>
    Third-party sites operate under their own privacy practices and terms. An affiliate link may
    allow a retailer to attribute a qualifying purchase to a referral.
  </p>
